{
  "lesson_id": "b1-b2_so_such_a_so_much_so_many",
  "level": "B1-B2",
  "title": "So, such (a), so much, so many",
  "description": "So и such усиливают смысл, но требуют разных конструкций. So much и so many показывают большое количество.",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-B1+-8-RU",
    "lesson_num": 8,
    "title": "Правила: So, such (a), so much, so many",
    "level": "B1-B2",
    "overview": "So и such усиливают смысл, но требуют разных конструкций. So much и so many показывают большое количество.",
    "main_rule": "So + adjective/adverb. Such + noun phrase. So much + uncountable. So many + plural countable.",
    "form": "so + adj/adv. such + a/an + adj + singular noun. such + plural/uncountable noun. so much + uncountable. so many + plural countable.",
    "when_why": "It was so difficult. / It was such a difficult task. / We had so much time. / There were so many questions.",
    "examples": "The service was so slow. → Сервис был таким медленным.\nThey are such helpful people. → Это такие полезные люди.\nIt was such an interesting idea. → Это была такая интересная идея.\nWe had so much time. → У нас было так много времени.\nThere were so many customers. → Было так много клиентов.",
    "special_cases": "С singular countable noun: such a/an + adjective + noun. С plural/uncountable: such + noun без a/an.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ so a difficult task → ✅ such a difficult task.\n❌ such an expensive → ✅ such an expensive car.\n❌ so many money → ✅ so much money.",
    "dont_confuse": "После so смотри на adjective/adverb. После such — noun phrase.",
    "quick_summary": "so + adjective/adverb.\nsuch + noun phrase.\nso much + uncountable.\nso many + plural countable."
  },
